#: ../../source/docs/common-do-return-path-start.rst:5
#: fb4edd0e2f1544b5beab57235d982396
msgid "Using DO_RETURN_PATH_START Mission Command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-return-path-start.rst:7
#: 8498340eea5a486a84f059026b22b6f5
msgid "While the :ref:`DO_LAND_START <common-do-land-start>` mission command provides a means of defining a \"landing sequence\" that can be directly jumped to for autolandings or failsafe actions, in some cases this direct path might result in breaching fences or flying into obstacles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-return-path-start.rst:9
#: 30a2e11be81441c4b543d4db5fbb7667
msgid "The DO_RETURN_PATH_START mission command can be used to mark a place or places in the mission sequence, before the :ref:`DO_LAND_START <common-do-land-start>`, that the vehicle should directly rejoin the mission path at the closet point on the mission leading toward the :ref:`DO_LAND_START <common-do-land-start>` sequence, rather than directly to the :ref:`DO_LAND_START <common-do-land-start>`. As shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-return-path-start.rst:14
#: 4c66fe692a214866ba8a32fa9d83ec3a
msgid "Imagine above that the vehicle takes off, flies to WP2 and 3, and if one were to fly up and look at the lake but then have a failsafe, the vehicle would fly directly back to the DO_LAND_START tag, crashing thru the tree, exclusion fence, etc. But if a DO_RETURN_PATH_START mission item is inserted after WP 3, then the vehicle would return to the mission path, proceed to the waypoint after the DO_LAND_START tag and LAND safely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-return-path-start.rst:16
#: 9841eeb5a58544efb97818a8fbf2aa1f
msgid "Multiple DO_RETURN_PATH_START items can be placed in the mission sequence to tailor the return. It is not necessary that the sequence include a :ref:`DO_LAND_START <common-do-land-start>`, but if it does, the return to the mission will occur after the DO_RETURN_PATH_START mission command but before the :ref:`DO_LAND_START <common-do-land-start>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-return-path-start.rst:19
#: 3c4ab3c843de4516ac9c07498ec93b1a
msgid "In Plane, set :ref:`RTL_AUTOLAND<RTL_AUTOLAND>` to 4 to use this."
msgstr ""
